Preserve existing scalar.rs Q/C Copy, constants, operators and signatures. Add Default zero, Q::try_new(i128,i128), fallible checked arithmetic and powers with Budget, C fallible analogues and Coefficient. Use native checked i128 arithmetic with GCD cancellation; intermediate overflow returns typed Overflow even when a mathematical result might fit; use arbitrary-precision backend explicitly when needed; legacy representable range excludes i128::MIN consistently with Q::new. Errors typed, never catch_unwind. Preserve old panic operators. Test zero errors, overflow, MIN normalization, budgets and small arithmetic crosschecks.

Q::try_new MUST normalize entirely natively: reject zero denominator, reduce unsigned_abs numerator/denominator by unsigned GCD, reject either reduced magnitude above i128::MAX, then restore numerator sign with positive denominator. Reducible MIN inputs are accepted; normalized MIN remains excluded. No dependency on exact.rs or arbitrary-precision constructors; scalar ownership must remain acyclic.
